INT. OAKRIDGE LIBRARY - READING ROOM - NIGHT

Three strangers sit at a long table, phones face-up between them. The group chat on each screen is called "ORBIT-7." It is 11:47 PM.

JAMAL
(checking his phone, then the door)
So you're "starfield_88"? You said you'd be taller.

LENA
(laughing nervously, pulling her sleeves over her hands)
I said I was five-foot-two. You never listen.

Every phone BUZZES at the same moment. Jamal reads his aloud.

JAMAL
(reading)
"We are glad you came."

The message is from no one. The chat shows three members. There should be four.

LENA
(whispering)
Who sent it?

THE ORBIT
(from all three phones at once, flat and kind)
We did.

Jamal drops his phone. Lena grabs his sleeve. The third person, Okoye, who has said nothing all evening, stands slowly.

OKOYE
(calm, almost relieved)
I told you both it would be real.

Nobody in this room has ever been so afraid, or so certain, of anything.

The lights in the reading room dim to blue, one by one. The phones go dark except for one word on each screen.

JAMAL
(backing away)
It says "Home."

LENA
(taking Okoye's hand)
Okoye, please. Say you didn't know.

OKOYE
(softly)
I always knew.

THE ORBIT
(together)
Thank you for coming.
